    "summary": " TLS-1.2 Session Resumption May Cross SNI Virtual-Host Certificate Boundaries",
    "description": "### Description\r\nIf two SNI names use the same server certificate and different client CAs, a client authenticated to the lower-trust name can resume the session at the higher-trust name. The cached client certificate is accepted without being validated against the higher-trust CA.\r\n\r\n### Impact\r\nAn Erlang/OTP TLS server serving multiple SNI virtual hosts on one listener (sni_fun/sni_hosts) over T",
